.SS "int32_t schultz_draw_list_init (\fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, \fBschultz_arena\fP * arena, uint32_t chunk_capacity)"

.PP
Prepares a draw list that appends into an arena\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The list to initialize\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIarena\fP The arena chunks are taken from\&. Must not be NULL and must outlive the list\&. 
.br
\fIchunk_capacity\fP Commands per chunk\&. Pass 0 to accept the default\&. Affects only how often a chunk is taken from the arena, never the list's capacity, which is unbounded\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK on success, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when list or arena is NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void schultz_draw_list_reset (\fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list)"

.PP
Drops every command from the list\&. Chunks already taken from the arena are kept and reused, so a list reset each frame settles and stops asking for memory\&. This does not reset the arena; the frame loop owns that\&. Pointers previously returned by schultz_draw_list_at become invalid\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The list to reset\&. NULL is accepted and does nothing\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t schultz_draw_list_count (const \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list)"

.PP
Counts commands in the list\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The list to query\&. NULL yields 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of commands appended since the last reset\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const \fBschultz_draw_cmd\fP * schultz_draw_list_at (const \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, uint32_t index)"

.PP
Returns the command at an index\&. Walks the chunk chain, so this is meant for tests and tooling\&. A backend should use schultz_draw_list_play instead\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The list to read\&. NULL yields NULL\&. 
.br
\fIindex\fP Zero based position in append order\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the command, valid until the list is reset or the arena is reset, or NULL when index is out of range\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_draw_list_overflowed (const \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list)"

