.SS "int32_t schultz_draw_group_begin (\fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, float opacity, \fBschultz_shadow\fP shadow)"

.PP
Starts a group\&. Everything drawn until the matching schultz_draw_group_end is composed into one picture, and that picture is blended in as a whole\&.
.PP
This is what makes a subtree fade as one thing\&. Without it, fading a panel and its contents means fading each of them, and everywhere they overlap is darker than it should be, because the same pixel was blended twice\&.
.PP
A group also casts the shadow, for the same reason: the subtree makes one picture, and one picture casts one shadow\&. Without that, a card with a title and a button would cast three shadows that overlap\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The list to add to\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIopacity\fP 0 for invisible, 1 for solid\&. Values outside are clamped by whatever draws them\&. 
.br
\fIshadow\fP The shadow the group casts\&. schultz_shadow_none for none, which is also what a fully transparent colour means\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

