\fIcmd\fP The command to copy in\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a NULL pointer, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY when a chunk could not be taken\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_draw_list_play (const \fBschultz_draw_list\fP * list, const \fBschultz_painter\fP * painter, \fBschultz_rect\fP bounds)"

.PP
Plays a command list into a backend\&. Calls begin, then one handler per command in append order, then end\&. Stops at the first handler error and returns it, still calling end so the backend can unwind\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIlist\fP The commands to play\&. Must not be NULL\&. An empty list is valid and still brackets the frame with begin and end\&. 
.br
\fIpainter\fP The backend to play into\&. Must not be NULL, and its vtable must be non-NULL with every entry filled in\&. 
.br
\fIbounds\fP The frame bounds, passed through to begin\&. Typically the surface or dirty region being painted\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK when every handler succeeded, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT for a NULL list or painter, a NULL vtable, an incomplete vtable, or an unrecognized command kind, or whatever error a handler returned\&. 
.RE
.PP

